b> use the entire hierarchy of classes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now, check the following chart to learn about the structures that we use with this modal verb:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subject </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal verb </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Main verb </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Complement </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">can</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">write</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">ASP.NET application codes in several languages. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">can't</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">write</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">ASP.NET application codes in several languages. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal verb </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subject </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Main verb </div> </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Complement </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Interrogative </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">you</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">write</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">ASP.NET application codes in several languages? </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "To clear the concept, HTTP is a stateless protocol that can process each code request separately, so that web applications can be available between server and users."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Understanding Stateless Protocols"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <b>stateless protocol</b> is a mechanism that allows making code requests and code responses independently. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When using <b>stateless protocols</b>, servers do not need to keep track of all session information users during a communication; in fact, each pair request-response acts separately.  </br></br>The most common examples of stateless protocols are:</br></br><i>Internet Protocol - IP</br>Hypertext Transfer Protocol - HTTP</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In some cases, <b>stateless protocols</b> cannot prevent some dangers of the internet such as spam or hacking. To prevent these types of situations, <b>stateless protocols</b> work together with stateful protocols to retain more information during communications. "}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob06img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "web framework "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a software that provides different tools to develop web applications "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: ASP.NET is a free web framework that allows developing dynamic websites, data-driven applications or web services for different computer devices. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "data driven application"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an application where data can control the flow of a program "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: ASP.NET is a free web framework that allows developing dynamic websites, data-driven applications or web services for different computer devices. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " server "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a computer program that can process and complete code requests "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The first format requires compilation before runtime, while in the second one, users can copy files straight to a server."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " stateless protocol "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an application that can execute code requests in an independent way,  such as IP or HTTP"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To clear the concept, HTTP is a stateless protocol that can process each code request separately, so that web applications can be available between server and users."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "store "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to save information  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: ASP.NET pages store information in two ways of interaction during a user session:  Page state and session state. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " keep track of "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to control information about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Then, web browsers can use cookies to keep track of the data provided in page state and session state."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a type company with not any information system."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about the needs of this company"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Design a brochure to inform what ASP.NET can provide to fulfill such needs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain your brochure to you instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I choose a company to promote ASP.NET."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about a company needs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design a brochure."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain my brochure to my instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le03ob06re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob06re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">ASP.NET is a free web framework that allows the development of dynamic websites, data-driven applications or web services for different computer devices. This software framework makes part of Microsoft's.Net, a platform where programmers can have access to different tools and databases to create HTLM sites. </br></br>\nOne of .NET framework's most remarkable features is that it uses Common Language Runtime, which makes it possible to write application codes in different types of computer languages such as Visual Basic, C#, and Jscript. Besides that, ASP.NET offers two kinds of web forms: on the one hand, a web application format; and, on the other hand, a website format. The first format requires compilation before runtime, while in the second one, users can copy files straight to a server. </br>"}, {"time": "64500", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob06re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">When using ASP.NET, web developers can put applications online in any kind of browser by means of HTTP protocols and HTTP commands that transfer information from servers to browsers. To clear the concept, HTTP is a stateless protocol that can process each code request separately, so that web applications can be available between server and users."}, {"time": "93000", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob06re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">ASP.NET pages store information in two ways of interaction during a user session:  Page state and session state. In page state, there is all the information concerning the user actions on a website; for example, the items a user puts in an online shopping cart. On the contrary, with the session state, you can find all the data referring to the user's navigation throughout different web pages; for instance, all the products the user checks before deciding to buy one. Then, web browsers can use cookies to keep track of the data provided in page state and session state."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le03ob06re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"_data": [], "contents": [], "type": "static", "template_override": 1, "id": 2, "title": ""}, {"_data": [], "contents": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 3, "title": ""}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n2le03ob06re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 4, "title": ""}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can understand written information about the ASP.NET web development platform. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can identify basic information about stateless protocols. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can locate the main ideas in a passage about technology. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What web development platforms do you know?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What computer languages can we use in a web development p